{
  "schema": "meridian.recipes.assignments/1",
  "_doc": [
    "Input of tools/py/gen_recipe_stubs.py (render spec 5.8.7 / 7.4). Resolution per def id: `overrides` (exact id) > `patterns` (fnmatch, top to bottom) > units only: `balance_to_view` of the balance archetype, then `ability_rules`.",
    "An id that matches nothing gets `default_archetype` and validate_recipes.py warns (V-RCP-02), so a renamed def never fails silently.",
    "`params` of a rule are written into the stub only where the used archetype declares them (`defaults`). `style: owner` = instantiate with the owning player's style.",
    "`fallbacks` (extension of the spec): while the view archetype named by a rule has no file in archetypes/, the stub uses the generic archetype named here (gen_*, veh_tank, inf_squad) so nothing ever falls back to the magenta placeholder box. As soon as archetypes/<name>.json exists, `gen_recipe_stubs.py` re-points every STUB (meta.stub = true) at it; hand-authored recipes are never touched.",
    "Structure kits: str_defense_adv `kit` = bulwark_cannon | lance_rail | sunwall | citadel_mortar | sea_spear | dragon_tooth | forge_cannon | bastion_tower; str_superweapon `kit` = halo_tower | billboard | sunflower | gantry_silo | hive_tower | assembly_hall | long_barrel | three_masts; neu_building `kit` = garrison | substation | outpost | depot | hospital | harbor | deposit (+ `heaps` 1..4)."
  ],
